 - Test: `rejects quantity reduction below allocated shipments`\n13. GET /shipments/{shipmentId}.quantity - Test: `includes quantity in shipment response`\n14. POST /shipments with quantity - Test: `includes quantity in shipment response`, `defaults quantity to 1 when not provided`\n15. POST /shipments allocation validation - Test: `rejects shipment allocation that exceeds order quantity`\n16. POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm - Test: `confirms shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED`, `rejects confirm when not in CREATED status`\n17. POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/deliver - Test: `delivers shipment from CONFIRMED to DELIVERED`, `rejects deliver when not in CONFIRMED status`\n18. POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel - Test: `cancels shipment from CREATED to CANCELLED`, `rejects cancel when not in CREATED status`, `releases cancelled shipment quantity for reallocation`\n19. GET /shipments with pagination - Test: `lists shipments with pagination` (X-Total-Count header verified)\n20. GET /customers/{customerId} 404 with error envelope - Test: `returns 404 with error envelope for an unknown customer`\n21. GET /customers with pagination - Test: `lists customers with pagination` (X-Total-Count header verified)\n22. GET /customers pagination validation - Test: `rejects invalid pagination parameters`\n\n**Rows uncovered:** None\n\n**Failing tests:** None\n\n**Verification command and result:**\n\n```\ncd /private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-53af3571-f75b-4a2e-9a7c-57f8214b0da5/sample-service && ./mvnw test\n```\n\nResult:\n```\nTests run: 37, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nSummary: All specification requirements from BE-005 are covered by tests that exercise the corresponding read paths after all writes the ticket allows. The implementation includes:\n- Order and shipment quantity fields (stored, default 1, validated)\n- Order fulfilment status computation (allocated, delivered, status enum)\n- Shipment allocation validation preventing exceeds\n- Shipment state transitions (confirm, deliver, cancel)\n- Order quantity amendment with conflict detection\n- Cancelled shipment quantity release for reallocation\n- Customer existence validation on order creation (422)\n- Customer 404 with error envelope\n- Pagination with X-Total-Count for orders, shipments, and customers\n- Fulfilment status filtering on order list","usage":{"total_tokens":34204,"tool_uses":15,"duration_ms":102523},"uuid":"6760c7b7-97f8-4208-9485-f3d1993c2421","session_id":"e34c75db-67e0-4ca9-8439-eacb7a0ca182"}
